Fig. 5 (a) and Fig. 5(b) show that the order of the identification performance of belt scale and stroke width is stable under the three color coding conditions, manifesting as the bar belt scale is better than the curved belt scale, and the thick stroke width is better than the thin stroke width. The difference between each level of the belt scale and stroke width is the most insignificant when the color is red, while is the most significant when the color is green. Fig. 5(c) shows that under the situation of using numeric box or not, the trend that the bar belt scale is better than the curved belt scale is obvious; under the situation of the curved belt scale, using numeric box or not shows no difference basically; while under the situation of bar belt scale, the difference between using numeric box and not is significant and shows the trend that using numeric box is better than not using numeric box.
B. Result analysis and discussion
1) Belt scale

The experiment results show that the identification performance of bar belt scale is better than curved belt scale. Although the curved belt scale meets the aesthetic requirements better, it is easier to cause the visual vertigo which results in the discomfort of human eye. Furthermore, the visual vertigo can also create a minor adverse mood of the subject to the curved belt scale. Therefore, it is not easy for the subject to accept the curved belt scale both psychologically and physiologically. This experiment result is identical with the fact that the GJB300–87 chooses bar belt scale as the standard [11] .
2) Numeric box

The experiment results show that the identification performance of using numeric box is better than not. As we all know, the numeric box next to the belt scale only plays an assistant role in helping the pilot to identify the information of speed and height. Thus, without the numeric box, the pilot can also get the information needed directly by observing the belt scale. However, the numeric box can help the pilot to distinguish the accurate value of the information more quickly and more accurately. This result is consistent with Ref. [5] .
3) Stroke width

The experiment results show that the identification performance of thick stroke width (2 mm) is higher than the thin stroke width (1 mm). It is easier to know that identifying flight information represented by the thin stroke width with the blue sky background is hard. This means that the size of stroke width has a notable effect on the information identification performance for the HUD interface, the present study only gives two different sizes of the stroke width, and more comparative experiments are needed in order to get more suitable size of the stroke width which can apply to the civil aircraft HUD. Ref. [12] has the proposed scope of the stroke width. Nevertheless it suits the Americans and may not be suitable for the Chinese.
4) Color

The experiment results show that the identification performance of the red is the best, followed by the yellow, and the green is the worst. The current experiment changes the displayed color of the abnormal message to improve the subject's identification performance. The identification performance of the yellow and red is notably higher than green. The probable reason is the different contrast between the target color and the background color. The displayed abnormal message with high color contrast to the background can easily stimulate human's visual receptors and make the pilot identify information faster and accurately. Therefore, changing the displayed color of the information can raise the pilot's alertness when designing the HUD interface. Furthermore the yellow is fit for the visual stimulus of the ordinary abnormal message and the red applies to the visual stimulus of the serious abnormal message.
5) Aircraft symbol

The experiment results show that the effect of aircraft symbol on the identification performance is insignificant. In fact, the function of the aircraft symbol is to help the pilot identify the roll attitude and pitch attitude, but the pilot can also determine the value of roll angle and pitch angle through the other symbols, therefore the aircraft symbol may play a minor role in assisting the pilot the get the required information. Another reason for the lack of differences among the identification performances is that the design levels of the four kind aircraft symbols are similar.
6) The interaction effects of different variables

The experiment results show that however the numeric box and the stroke width change, the interaction effects between the belt scale and the color are significant on identification correct rate. The trend of the two kinds of belt scales' identification performances is almost the same under the three colors conditions, the difference is that they are the most significant when the color is green and the most insignificant when the color is red. However the numeric box and the belt scale change, the interaction effects between color and stroke width are significant on the identification correct rate. The trend of the two kinds of stroke widths' identification performances is almost the same under the three colors, their difference is the most significant when the color is green and the most insignificant when the color is red. When the abnormal message is displayed in red, the differences between them are not that obvious, which on the other hand confirms that red is the most suitable color coding method for the abnormal message display.
SECTION V.
Conclusions

The ergonomics design and evaluation of HUD visual coding is investigated in the present study. The HUD layout and information display simulation model is developed by OpenGL and VS2008. Based on it, the ergonomics experiment is carried out. According to the results of data processing and analysis, some conclusions about the ergonomics design of the HUD visual coding has been drawn: The bar rather than curved belt scale should be chosen as the information format; when identifying the exact value is needed, the belt scale should be coupled with the numeric box; when the blue sky is the background, the stroke width of information should be appropriately thicker. As the abnormal message appears, the red should be used as the serious abnormal message, the yellow as the ordinary abnormal message, and the green should not be used as the color coding method of the abnormal message; the four aircraft symbols are all suitable for applying to the HUD visual coding.

